DSH-Android patch 18: llm-service-lite (vendored @snnh/dsh-llm-service-lite 0.2.1), provider-declared
request headers and a "model not available to this account" error code. Applies on top of 14, 16, 17.

Route headers (#32). A route could declare static `headers` only. Some providers want more:
OpenCode Go (opencode.ai/zen/go/v1) answers chat requests without `x-opencode-session` with
"Request is missing x-opencode-session … INVALID_REQUEST" (its /models works without), and a
gateway header may be a secret that must not sit in configuration. New route fields:
 - `sessionHeader`: header name; every model request of a harness session carries it with
   sha256("dsh-android/session-header/v1\0" + route + "\0" + sessionId)[0..32] (hex): stable for
   the session (and across engine restarts / resume), unlinkable to the session id, different per
   session and per route. A request without a session id, and every model listing, gets a fresh
   random id.
 - `headerEnv`: header name → credential reference, resolved per request like `apiKeyEnv`
   (credentials service, else launch environment); unset → MISSING_CREDENTIAL. Never replaces the
   key's own authorization / x-api-key.
 - `userAgent`: product token put in front of the harness User-Agent (`DSH-Android/0.2.6
   deepseek-harness/<v> (+url)`), unless the route declares a User-Agent header itself.
Final headers are lower-cased, so a declared header replaces a default of the same name whatever
its case. Model listings (registerModelDiscovery) send the same static / secret headers, the
User-Agent token and a fresh session id.

MODEL_NOT_AVAILABLE. A 403 "Model.AccessDenied" (DashScope), "您无权访问" (Zhipu 1220), "not
available for your account" (SiliconFlow 30011), "does not have access to model" (OpenAI project),
and Ark's 404 ModelNotOpen "has not activated the model" were AUTH or INVALID_REQUEST, so the app
told the user the key was wrong / the address was wrong. A 4xx (not 401/402/429) that says the model
is not activated (未开通 / ModelNotOpen / not activated), or that access is denied (on a 403, or
without "does not exist" wording), is now `MODEL_NOT_AVAILABLE` (not retried) with message
`llm-service-lite: model "<id>" is not available to this account: <server text>`. Exhausted
balance stays QUOTA; key complaints and region blocks keep their codes; "does not exist or you do
not have access" on a 404 (OpenAI) stays INVALID_REQUEST. Exports MODEL_NOT_AVAILABLE_CODE,
isModelUnavailable, routeHeaders, sessionToken for tests.

